We are Team CRICKSTATS.

3
00:00:03,396 --> 00:00:05,283
Our team lead is A.G.

4
00:00:05,283 --> 00:00:09,245
Vasheela Afrin, and the team members are R.

5
00:00:09,245 --> 00:00:10,754
Sivasakthi and S.

6
00:00:10,754 --> 00:00:11,226
Subha.

7
00:00:11,226 --> 00:00:15,000
This is our project demonstration video.

8
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:21,995
The name of our project is the Cricket Player Performance Tracking Application, called CRICKSTATS.

9
00:00:21,995 --> 00:00:30,000
It is a Salesforce Lightning application built with custom objects, relationships, roll-up summaries and flows.

10
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:37,870
The purpose of this project is to capture match by match performance of cricket players in one place.

11
00:00:37,870 --> 00:00:47,000
It replaces scattered spreadsheets and manual calculations, and it helps coaches and managers make better decisions.

12
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,802
Now the use and benefits.

13
00:00:48,802 --> 00:01:03,000
The application keeps data accurate through relationships, calculates career totals automatically, reduces manual work with flows, gives insightful reports, and is easy to use and to scale.

14
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:06,483
Now let us see how the project works.

15
00:01:06,483 --> 00:01:10,741
Step one is the Salesforce Developer account.

16
00:01:10,741 --> 00:01:21,000
We signed up for a free Developer Edition org, verified our email, set a password, and logged in to Setup.

17
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:23,209
Step two is object creation.

18
00:01:23,209 --> 00:01:28,199
In Setup, we opened Object Manager and created custom objects.

19
00:01:28,199 --> 00:01:30,490
Player stores each cricketer.

20
00:01:30,490 --> 00:01:35,154
Match Performance stores one player's result in one match.

21
00:01:35,154 --> 00:01:39,000
Team is an optional object that groups players.

22
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:42,636
Step three is tabs and the Lightning App.

23
00:01:42,636 --> 00:01:58,000
We created a custom tab for each object, then in App Manager we created the CRICKSTATS Lightning App, added the tabs to its navigation, and assigned it to user profiles.

24
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:00,953
Step four is fields and relationships.

25
00:02:00,953 --> 00:02:04,226
Player has role, age and a lookup to Team.

26
00:02:04,226 --> 00:02:17,000
Match Performance has match date, opponent, runs scored, balls faced, wickets and overs bowled, and it is connected to Player with a Master-Detail relationship.

27
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:19,726
Step five is the roll-up summary.

28
00:02:19,726 --> 00:02:25,520
Because of the Master-Detail relationship, Player has roll-up fields.

29
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:28,587
Total Runs is the sum of runs scored.

30
00:02:28,587 --> 00:02:31,569
Total Wickets is the sum of wickets.

31
00:02:31,569 --> 00:02:35,999
Matches Played counts the match performance records.

32
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:37,596
Step six is flows.

33
00:02:37,596 --> 00:02:42,760
We created a Record-Triggered Flow on Match Performance.

34
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:52,995
When a new record is created, the flow checks the values and performs an action such as an update or an email.

35
00:02:52,995 --> 00:02:56,000
Then we tested and activated it.

36
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,462
Now the live demo.

37
00:02:57,462 --> 00:03:05,118
We open the CRICKSTATS app, add a new player, then add match performances for that player.

38
00:03:05,118 --> 00:03:12,000
Watch how the total runs, total wickets and matches played update automatically.

39
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,894
This is the final output.

40
00:03:13,894 --> 00:03:27,000
We have a working CRICKSTATS Lightning App with players, match performances and teams, automatic career totals, an automated flow, and reports to analyse performance.

41
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,872
Thank you for watching.

42
00:03:28,872 --> 00:03:35,680
This was CRICKSTATS, the Cricket Player Performance Tracking Application, by A.G.

